  "Welcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter The Practice and the Dojo. Before code synthesis models and automated agents, developers met face to face to establish standards of craftsmanship. Today we rewatch Episode 11: Justin Searls from SCNA 2012 (2012).",
  "Justin Searls was a major recurring voice at SCNA Chicago, using sharp humor and deep empathy to help developers laugh at their own architectural excesses.",
  "What inspired Justin Searls to challenge dogma in test-driven development? How did Test Double pioneer a humane, empathetic model of consulting that prioritized team health over rigid doctrine? What principles guided Justin Searls when this conversation was recorded? How do those lessons inform the software systems we design today?",
  "Roll archive footage (YouTube ID: 6JB7o8I4Uy4). Watch for the unvarnished hallway exchanges, the emphasis on craft over speed, and the sheer enthusiasm of engineers taking responsibility for their software.",
  "Dogma is the enemy of effectiveness. As AI enters the software lifecycle, blindly applying 2010 testing rituals without understanding their purpose creates brittle friction. When implementation is cheap, verification and clarity become everything. We cannot accept the mirage of competence. Let us examine the terminal contracts directly.",
  "Thank you for joining today's session. Full transcripts, provenance notes, and companion research are available at just3ws.com. In our next broadcast, we explore Episode 12. Until next time, keep your feedback loops fast and your code humane."
]